        "reason": null,
        "diff": "--- /dev/null\n+++ /home/agent/workspace/claim.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+# Claim: Distributivity of doubling over addition\n+\n+## Function\n+\n+Define a small arithmetic function `double` over the integers:\n+\n+    double(n) = n + n\n+\n+## Informal Claim\n+\n+Doubling distributes over integer addition. That is, for **all** integers `a` and `b`:\n+\n+    double(a) + double(b) = double(a + b)\n+\n+In words: doubling two numbers separately and then adding the results gives the\n+same value as adding the numbers first and then doubling the sum.\n+\n+## Reasoning sketch\n+\n+Each side simplifies to `2a + 2b` by the commutativity and associativity of\n+integer addition, so the two sides must agree for every choice of `a` and `b`.\n+\n+## Formalization intent\n+\n+This claim is intended to be verified formally, e.g., as a proof assistant\n+lemma (Lean/Coq/Isabelle) or an SMT-checked assertion, stating:\n+\n+    ∀ a b : ℤ, double a + double b = double (a + b)\n"
      }
